      "## Frequently asked questions",
      "### How many questions should a backend developer interview include?",
      "Five to seven per round, across a two- or three-round loop. Depth on a few questions — with follow-ups like \"what breaks first?\" — tells you far more than rushing through fifteen.",
      "### Should backend interviews include live coding?",
      "Yes, but make it realistic. Building or fixing a small API endpoint, or debugging a failing test, predicts real work better than algorithm puzzles for most backend roles.",
