      "## Frequently asked questions",
      "### What should a frontend developer interview include?",
      "A practical coding task, questions on JavaScript and your framework, CSS and layout, performance, accessibility, and a behavioral round. Three rounds is enough for most mid-level roles.",
      "### Is a take-home test better than live coding for frontend roles?",
      "Both work. A short take-home (two to three hours, paid if longer) shows how they structure real code. Live coding shows how they think and communicate. Pick one, and keep it realistic.",
      "### How much should I focus on React-specific questions?",
      "Enough to confirm they can work in your stack, but weight fundamentals higher. A developer who understands JavaScript, the browser, and accessibility learns any framework quickly.",
